The\n\u2018TF mRNA peaks between 2 and 4h after LPS treat-\nment and decreases to baseline by 8h after LPS treat-\nment. At present, there is litle information which\ndescribes how synthesis and degradation of TF is\nregulated.\nIn an earlier report, low concentrations of phorbol\nmyristate acetate (PMA) were shown to stimulate\n\nThe anthors ar with che Deparement of Pathology and Microbiology,\nMedical Center, Omaha, USA. Addren corespondence to Jab . Broo\n\nof Pachelogy, 10250 ast Dahovs Avenue, Denver, CO 80231, USA,\n\n1 1994 Rapid Commuriains of Oxford Lad\n\nexpression of tissue factor in human monocytes, while\nconcentrations of PMA greater than 10\u00b0 M induced a\nrapid decrease in monocyte-associated tissue factor\nactivity This report demonstrates that staurosporine,\nan inhibitor of protein kinase C, enhances the stimu\nlatory effect of PMA on TF expression in monocytes\nand blocks the inhibition of tissue factor expression by\nrelatively high concentrations of PMA. In addition, it\nis shown that staurosporine prolongs and enhances\nexpression of TFin monocytes treated with LPS. These\ndata support hypotheses that protein kinases are\ninvolved in control of the down-regulation of tissue\nfactor activity as well as its induction.\n\nMaterials and methods\nReagents\nStaurosporine (Calbiochem Corp., San Diego, CA)\nand calphostin (Kamiya Biochemical Co., Thousand\nOaks, CA) were prepared as concentrated stock sol-\ntutions in dimethyl sulphoxide (DMSO) and stored at\n4#C. Phorbol myristate acetate (PMA; LC Services,\nWoburn, MA) was prepared as a concentrated stock:\n\nUniverty of Nebrasta Medical Centr, and Veterans Administration\nna, MD, PhD, Colorado Permanente Medical Group, PC, Department\n\nBlood Coagulation and Fibrinolysis, ol, 1998. 929", "words": [{"text": "lod", "x0": 79, "y0": 52, "x1": 100, "y1": 60, "conf": 53.0}, {"text": "Carlton", "x0": 103, "y0": 53, "x1": 163, "y1": 62, "conf": 35.0}, {"text": "and", "x0": 149, "y0": 42, "x1": 164, "y